{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969622-has-anyone-tried-the-weird-science-rules-from-the-chronicler-s-guide","id":969622,"title":"Has anyone tried the Weird Science rules from the Chronicler's Guide?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T20:23:04-07:00","id":969622,"title":"Has anyone tried the Weird Science rules from the Chronicler's Guide?","content":"I was wondering, has anyone played Mage using the mad science hack from the Chronicler's Guide? When I mention how I wish I could play a major template mad scientist, a lot of people have mentioned this. So, is it good? Has anyone used it? Has anyone added to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:19:02-07:00","id":969692,"title":"","content":"I made simple Persistant Condition that works with most of this rules for 2E as written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Instrumentalist </b><b>( Persistent, Awakened only )</b><br /> You character, even if technically mage, does not see that her miracles are coming from her. Whatever if she is die hard scientists, seeing her magic as advanced technology, or dedicated priest, believing they are granted by her patrons \u2013 she cannot 'cast' any spell without utilizing appropriate Yantras. She cannot force herself to acknowledge that Supernal power comes from her and by this, is slave to tools and ceremonies. When character tries to cast without at least one Yantra in accordance with its worldview, spell is automatic Dramatic Failure \u2013 resolve it\u2019s effects on character and environment in accordance.<br /> It\u2019s very popular affliction in Nameless mages or some parts of Free Council. What\u2019s even more disturbing, large parts of Banishers are under it.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Specific background. Wisdom loss.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Confrontation with reality of being mage. Dramatic Failure on spellcasting roll ( choose player and ST combined )<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character gives a 'tribute' for higher force or analyze the 'scientific basis' of his miracles (Arcane). Character undermines the Truth about the origins of magic in other sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:33:49-07:00","id":971014,"title":"","content":"Has anyone considered houseruling that a fair portion of Awakened are actually operating using this framework, meaning that players could play either a Mage or a mad scientist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:33:30-07:00","id":971140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969622-has-anyone-tried-the-weird-science-rules-from-the-chronicler-s-guide?p=971014#post971014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone considered houseruling that a fair portion of Awakened are actually operating using this framework, meaning that players could play either a Mage or a mad scientist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan this for my long future historical Nameless War game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Basiclly, PCs will <i>create</i> Free Council, and Council in my settings is mix of proper wizards, wierd psychics and mad scientists, and anything Awakened related.<br /> <br /> Still, never used alternative template, as did not dwell in to variety of Free Council with my normal games as I have gameplay full of main plot, subplots, Diamond infighting and Seers conspiracies. Maybe someday when I will need Libertines of technomagic variety, someday,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:57:54-07:00","id":971256,"title":"","content":"Also, remember that 'lower than Awakened' people with talents are also parts of Diamond Orders from centuries...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971253#post971253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is like MAsc, but we try to remember that the Orders are full of Status 1 hedge magicians and psychics rather than saying so in one book (Sorcerer Revised) and ignoring it thereafter.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:55:54-07:00","id":971657,"title":"","content":"Eh. That doesn't address my &quot;mages aren't monstrous enough and hedge wizards just feel like shittier mages&quot; problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:30:05-07:00",